<title>AUSTRIA: Iraq says OPEC need do no more to make room for Iraq.</title>
<headline>Iraq says OPEC need do no more to make room for Iraq.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of the Iraqi delegation to OPEC's Wednesday's meeting Osama al-Hiti said on his arrival here on Tuesday that the group did not need to take any more action to fit in Iraqi production.</p>
<p>&quot;They did more than enough already,&quot; Hiti told reporters</p>
<p>&quot;No, I think that it is more than enough,&quot; when asked if OPEC need do more.</p>
<p>When asked on prospective Iraqi volumes under the terms of the U.N. Iraq oil-for-food deal he said &quot;it all depends on the pricing formula and the pricing.&quot;  </p>
<p>At the last OPEC meeting in June this year Iraq was awarded an extra allocation of 800,000 barrels per day to accommodate exports under the planned U.N. deal.</p>
<p>Iraq on Tuesday agreed to all the U.N. terms for the deal.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
